Think of sed as a tool for finding and modifying text programmatically
sed = stream editor

lt-befisc_t032@LT-BE043 28-sed % sed 's/True/False/' config.txt
DEBUG=False
DATABASE=old_database


Read config.txt, make the replacement in the output, and print that modified result to the terminal.
It does not modify the actual file.

sed -i '' 's/True/False/' config.txt

this is used to actually update in the config

